# 024-forest-text.lua

Draws a reader's forest (from 023) as plain text, one room per line, with
box-drawing branches.  A room whose parent was said but never received
ends with `   (inside a room you are not in)`.

| function | takes | gives |
|---|---|---|
| `lines(forest)` | a forest from `visible_forest` | list of strings, one per room |
| `text(forest)` | a forest | one string: the lines joined with line breaks, ending in one |

Example output:

    home
    └── ritz
        └── programming
